{"dir": "s2c", "type": "say", "id": "teachback-8-10", "text": "anything from the UK subsidiary needs second approval from the controller before booking. Is that how it works?", "kind": "teachback", "lang": "en", "step_id": "s10", "_at": 1791096508900.116}
{"dir": "s2c", "type": "map_updated", "workflow_id": "wf_purchase_invoice_processing_erpnext_75c2ae", "version": 7, "_at": 1791096570567.695}
{"dir": "s2c", "type": "say", "id": "debrief-9", "text": "Got it — the rule now says: New equipment with an amount over 5,000 is capex: it must never be booked to small tools — use Plants and Machineries with the Production cost center. Maintenance and repairs stay an expense even above 5,000. Anything else, or is that how it works?", "kind": "debrief", "lang": "en", "_at": 1791096571166.775}
